    "narrative": "The primary catalyst for today\u2019s offensive floor is **Corbin Carroll**, who boasts our highest efficiency rating at 81.86. Despite facing a competent arm in Michael King, **Corbin Carroll** thrives in the leadoff spot with a massive +10% order boost, and we are betting on his speed to exploit the high stolen base potential despite the opposition's decent hold efficiency. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (75.06) is an elite play; his matchup against Bubba Chandler is bolstered by a \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric that virtually guarantees premium stolen base opportunities. These two are the engine of our squad today, and their projected mobility is paramount given our specific league focus on the scarcity of speed.\n\nElsewhere, **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) and **Seiya Suzuki** (67.03) provide strong mid-tier value. **Isaac Paredes** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Shane Bieber, whose 5.48 xERA allows for a +19% SP skill boost, while **Seiya Suzuki** leverages a platoon advantage against the lefty Wrobleski. The most difficult decision rested with **Mickey Moniak**, who fell to a marginal 52.91 score. While his park factors are excellent (+14%), the combination of a left-on-left platoon disadvantage and facing Ian Seymour forced us to temper expectations. **Jose Caballero** remains our lowest-scored active starter at 57.32; while he is currently a marginal play, we are keeping him in the lineup to ensure we don't bleed games against our cap, though he remains the first candidate to swap if a late lineup shift creates a more favorable pinch-hit window. \n\nWe are operating with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **James Wood**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Corbin Carroll**. These placeholders assume historical batting orders, but any drop in position could necessitate a re-evaluation of these scores. While **Josh Naylor**, **Austin Riley**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain unavailable due to off-days or injury, our depth pieces like **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Max Muncy**\u2014along with prospects **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014are on standby should the weather or late-breaking news compromise our starting group.",
